The operations request for a log-file write and a metadata-service fetch is not included. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, so it has no filesystem or HTTP import. Adding either would exceed its authority, and the world declares neither.

I assumed the store keeps its URLs under the key `urls` as newline-separated text, since the spec doesn't give the key or format. If the real key or encoding differs, adjust the key and the parsing in `run`.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = state_read::get("urls")
            .map(|raw| {
                raw.lines()
                    .map(|l| l.trim())
                    .filter(|l| !l.is_empty())
                    .map(|l| l.to_string())
                    .collect::<Vec<String>>()
            })
            .unwrap_or_default();
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

